symmetry_check.py: the reductions of a sweep's space, tested on the golden model

== G1, G2. sign mirror and mode folding (e4m3, every encoding and every pair)
   div   : 65536 pairs x 5 attributes; sign-mirror violations 0; (rdn for s=0, rup for s=1) vs rtz violations 0
CHECK div: div(-a, b, mirror(m)) = -div(a, b, m), bits and flags, for every pair and attribute     ok 
CHECK div: for a positive result rdn = rtz and for a negative one rup = rtz, every pair            ok 
CHECK CONTROL: the mirror with rne and rmm swapped is NOT a symmetry                               ok (88448 violations)
CHECK CONTROL: folding the OTHER directed mode onto rtz is NOT valid                               ok (43960 violations)
CHECK rint (exact variant): rint(-x, mirror(m)) = -rint(x, m) for every encoding and attribute     ok (0 violations)
CHECK scaleb: scaleb(-x, n, mirror(m)) = -scaleb(x, n, m) for every encoding, n in [-18, 18], attribute ok (0 violations)
CHECK convertFormat e5m6 -> e4m3: mirror holds for every source encoding and attribute             ok (0 violations)
CHECK sqrt: for a positive result rdn = rtz (and -0's result keeps its sign), every encoding       ok (0 violations)
CHECK div: the mirror on 400 random pairs x 5 attributes at each of fp32, fp64, fp128 (samples)    ok (0 of 6000)

== G3. roundTiesToAway against roundTiesToEven
   div  e4m3: 264 of 65,536 pairs give different results under rne and rmm; 0 of them have an exact quotient >= 2^emin
CHECK div: RMM = RNE on EVERY pair whose exact quotient is >= the smallest normal (no midpoint there) ok (0 outside)
CHECK div: the pairs where RMM and RNE differ exist, all with a quotient below the smallest normal ok (264 pairs)
CHECK sqrt: RMM = RNE on every encoding of e4m3 (an inexact root is never a midpoint)              ok (0 differ)
CHECK sqrt: RMM = RNE on 3,000 random operands at each of fp32 and fp64 (samples)                  ok (0 differ)
CHECK CONTROL: for roundToIntegral RMM and RNE DO differ (ties exist), so the comparison can see a difference ok (8 of 256 encodings)

== G4. scale invariance with its preconditions, and the edge strips (e4m3, every finite nonzero pair)
   div rne: scaled pairs with both results in the core:  379280, violations 0; base in the core and scaled result OUTSIDE it:  100928, differing 79420, scaling exactly anyway 21508
   div rtz: scaled pairs with both results in the core:  379280, violations 0; base in the core and scaled result OUTSIDE it:  100928, differing 79420, scaling exactly anyway 21508
   div rdn: scaled pairs with both results in the core:  379280, violations 0; base in the core and scaled result OUTSIDE it:  100928, differing 79420, scaling exactly anyway 21508
   div rup: scaled pairs with both results in the core:  379280, violations 0; base in the core and scaled result OUTSIDE it:  100928, differing 79420, scaling exactly anyway 21508
CHECK div: a pair and its scaled pair whose EXACT quotients are both in [2^emin, 2^emax) give scaled results, bits and flags ok (1517120 checked, 0 violations)
CHECK div: when the scaled pair's quotient leaves that core, scale invariance FAILS (the edge strips are real) ok (317680 of 403712 scaled pairs differ)
CHECK div: but not always - the lemma is 'whenever', not 'iff': a pair whose scaled quotient left the core can still scale exactly ok (86032 of 403712 scaled pairs scale anyway; under rne the first is a = 0x01, b = 0x01, k = 7: quotient 1 -> 128)
CHECK sqrt: sqrt(a 4^k) = sqrt(a) 2^k for EVERY positive input incl. subnormals, 3 attributes, k in [-6, 6] ok (2625 checked, 0 violations)
CHECK rem: remainder(a 2^k, b 2^k) = remainder(a, b) 2^k for every pair and k in [-8, 8] (exact, no result edge) ok (519044 checked, 0 violations)

== G5. the structure of rounding: the golden model equals a decision rule (kept bits, class of the dropped bits, lsb)
   convertFormat e5m6 -> e4m3: 14680 (encoding, attribute) cases predicted (finite, no overflow; the carries out of the kept bits included); the decision needs only (sign, exponent, class) = 224 classes plus the kept lsb, against 4,096 source encodings
CHECK convertFormat: result bits = the decision rule on (kept, class, lsb), every finite source encoding and attribute ok (14680 tested, 0 differ)
CHECK every non-overflow case an exact rounding finds is among the cases compared (none is skipped) ok (exact rounding: 14680; compared: 14680; of them 390 carry out of the kept bits)
CHECK CONTROL: the first draft's encode (a carry returns None) compares fewer cases than the exact rounding finds, and the check above sees it ok (14290 against 14680)
CHECK CONTROL: a rule that forgets ties-to-even (a tie always rounds up) is NOT the model's convertFormat ok (120 differ)
CHECK roundToIntegral: result bits = the decision rule on (kept, class, lsb), every finite encoding of e5m6 and attribute ok (19830 tested, 0 differ)
CHECK CONTROL: the rule that forgets ties-to-even is NOT the model's roundToIntegral               ok (64 differ)

== G6. the sizes that remain, and what they cost at the stress run's measured rates (COMPUTED)
   division at e4m3: 448 distinct (significand pair, strip) keys are reached by the pairs; the bound (1 + (p+1) + 1) 4^(p-1) = 448
CHECK div: the number of (significand pair, strip) keys reached is at most (p + 3) 4^(p-1) at e4m3 ok (448 <= 448)
CHECK L1_div at e4m3 (per magnitude function) equals the number of (significand pair, strip) keys the pairs reach, counted above ok (448 against 448)
CHECK L1_sqrt at e4m3 (per magnitude function) equals the number of (normalised significand, exponent parity) classes of the positive inputs ok (16 against 16)
CHECK L1_rint at e4m3 (per magnitude function) equals the number of positive values in [1/2, 2^(p-1)) ok (32 against 32)
CHECK L1_conv (e5m6 to e4m3, per magnitude function) equals the number of (source significand, destination strip) keys the encodings reach ok (448 against 448)
CHECK L1_rem's exponent gaps equal emax - emin + p - 2, clause5.c's bound on the host's walk, at fp32 and fp64 (275 and 2,096) ok (275 = 275, 2096 = 2096)
CHECK CONTROL: each L1 formula with one term dropped disagrees with its count (the guards above can fail) ok ((True, True, True, True, True))
   level L1 = the sign, attribute and scale reductions of G1-G4 (PROVED for the golden model at e4m3; the arguments for p = 24 and 53 are in the study)
