   div32's reduced space: 5699868278390784 = 3 magnitude functions x 27 strips-and-core x 2^46; one quad needs 22.3 years (L0: 3.0e5 years)
CHECK div32's reduced sweep is under 100 quad-years (the raw one is over 300,000)                  ok (22.3 y)
CHECK every reduced space is smaller than its raw space                                            ok 

   level L2 (PLAUSIBLE, a structural assumption about the implementation; G5 shows the model's structure): the result depends on
   (sign, exponent, class of the dropped bits, kept lsb, kept all-ones), so a representative per class plus a walking-ones set over
   the dropped and kept bits covers it. conv64to32: 281 exponents x 4 classes x (lsb 2 x all-ones 2 + 52 walking bits) x 2 signs x 3 magnitude
   functions = 377664 cases; at the measured conv64to32 rate of 6.2 M/s (a host item: one core) that is 0.06 seconds
CHECK conv64to32's class-level sweep (a few hundred thousand cases) takes seconds, not years       ok (377664 cases)

symmetry_check: every CHECK held
